Memorandum of Understanding between the City of Cheyenne and the 37 Helicopter
th
Squadron of the United States Air Force for use of the Belvoir Ranch for helicopter training.  James
Perrott Macneil made comments in opposition to opening up the Belvoir Ranch for purposes of the
proposed Memorandum of Understanding or for any other use.  Reporting for Finance Committee,
Mr. Brown moved to approve, seconded by Mr. Valdez.  Mr. Brown, seconded by Mr. Pierson,
moved to amend page 2, Section B, by inserting a new subsection h. to read as follows:  “The
Government understands and agrees that helicopter landing areas may be restricted or curtailed by
the Owner in order to avoid conflicts with wind data collection and/or environmental assessments
which may be occurring on the Belvoir Ranch.  The Owner agrees to provide the Government with
maps, grid coordinates or legal descriptions indicating landing areas being impacted by on going
studies.”.  Motion to amend carried.  Voting “yes” -- all members of the governing body.  Main
motion as amended carried.  Voting “yes” -- all members of the governing body. (#5792)
